This program listens for beacons sent from wireless access points
in the range of your wireless station. Once received the program
extracts the BSSID of the AP and transmits deauthentication packets
using the broadcast MAC address. This results to the disconnection
of all clients connected to the AP at the time of the attack. This
is essencially a WiFi DoS attack tool created for educational
purposes only. It works only in Linux and requires wireless card
drivers capable of injecting packets in wireless networks.

How to use it: Just run it as root, passing the interface and any options
in any order (options and the interface may be mixed). It will
automatically put your interface in monitor
mode and it will listen at channel range 1-14. If there is no AP in the
channel, it will change channel every 1 second, or else it will start
the attack which it takes approximately 30 seconds. After that it will
change channel.


compile:
    make

install:
    make PREFIX=/usr install

ARM cross-compile:
    make CROSS_COMPILE=arm-none-linux-gnueabi-


Android (NDK cross-compile)
---------------------------
Builds native ARM executables for Android. This program needs root,
monitor-mode capable WiFi chipset, and raw packet (AF_PACKET) access, all
of which are uncommon on stock Android hardware. Root your device and
check that your WiFi driver supports monitor mode + injection.

Prerequisites: Android NDK r29 (installed at /opt/android-ndk here, via
`yay -S android-ndk`).

Build (both arm64-v8a and armeabi-v7a):
    make android            # uses $(NDK), default /opt/android-ndk

or directly:
    /opt/android-ndk/ndk-build -j$(nproc) \
        NDK_PROJECT_PATH=. \
        APP_BUILD_SCRIPT=jni/Android.mk \
        NDK_APPLICATION_MK=jni/Application.mk

Clean: make android-clean

Output executables (Android PIE, API 21):
    libs/arm64-v8a/wificurse
    libs/armeabi-v7a/wificurse

Deploy: push to device, chmod +x, run as root:
    adb push libs/arm64-v8a/wificurse /data/local/tmp/wificurse
    adb shell su -c "chmod 755 /data/local/tmp/wificurse"
    adb shell su -c "/data/local/tmp/wificurse wlan0"

Device notes
------------
iw.c talks cfg80211/nl80211 over raw netlink (no libnl needed, the NDK
does not ship it), so it works on modern drivers that dropped the legacy
WEXT ioctls (SIOCSIWMODE/SIOCSIWFREQ).

On Qualcomm qcacld devices (e.g. Redmi Note 12 "topaz"/bengal) the driver must be
put into monitor mode via con_mode before the
program runs, otherwise SET_INTERFACE(monitor) and raw packet access will
not work. From a root adb shell (recipe from kimocoder/qualcomm_android_monitor_mode):

    ip link set wlan0 down
    echo 4 > /sys/module/wlan/parameters/con_mode
    ip link set wlan0 up

Then run wificurse. To restore normal WiFi afterwards:

    ip link set wlan0 down
    echo 0 > /sys/module/wlan/parameters/con_mode
    ip link set wlan0 up
    svc wifi enable   # framework may force-restart anyway
